  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - CARTAGENA WASTEWATER TREATMENT SYSTEM START-UP, through Government of Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $513,000 grant funds a technical assistance for the launch of a comprehensive wastewater treatment system for the city of Cartagena on Colombia&apos;s Caribbean cost. The main objectives are to provide technical assistance in integrating sub systems and the startup of the new wastewater system in Cartagena, and the creation of an enviromental water quality baseline and water quality monitoring program. This project will have a significant postive public health and environmental benefit for Cartagena and also support its tourism industry, the most important economic driver for the city.</narrative>
  </description>
